text:
kidai-hub README · ✨ What it is：- 🗂️ **Unified container** — Kidai plugins register their panel into `kidai-hub.tabs`; the hub renders them in a dynamic tab bar, so one hub covers every Kidai tool;
- 🚀 **One click from the sidebar** — the "Kidai Hub" button sits above the 设置 (Settings) button in the home sidebar and opens the full-screen hub;
- 🧩 **Natural fallback** — when `kidai-hub` is not installed, each Kidai plugin falls back to its own standalone entry, with no loss of functionality;
- 🔌 **Pure browser container** — the host half is a no-op; all UI lives in the client, with no change to DSH host logic.

kidai-hub README · 🎯 Features：- **Full-screen hub page** — header (title + close button) + dynamic tab bar + scrollable content area `kidh_body`;
- **Tab slot `kidai-hub.tabs`** — kind **keyed**, scope `root`; one `key` per Kidai plugin (usually the plugin id), ordered by `order`;
- **Header action slot `kidai-hub.header.action`** — for plugins to append their own actions to the hub header;
- **Live updates** — tab register/unregister reflects in the hub header immediately, with no blank frame (the active tab falls back to the first one);
- **Brand colors** — known plugins get a dedicated brand gradient; the rest derive a stable default color from their `key`;
- **Bilingual** — Chinese / English READMEs.
